{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"- **Written policies:** Adopt and implement procedures governing basket construction and acceptance in the best interests of the ETF and shareholders.\n- **Custom-basket controls:** Establish detailed construction/acceptance parameters, including a process for revising or deviating from them. Specify titles or roles of investment-adviser employees required to review each custom basket for compliance. Rule 38a-1 adds board-approved compliance policies, CCO oversight and annual review—not board approval of individual baskets.\n- **Records:** Retain written authorized-participant agreements and, for every exchanged basket, holding identifiers, quantities, cash-balancing amounts and AP identity. For custom baskets, record that designation and a statement of compliance with custom-basket policies. Retention: five years, first two easily accessible.\n- **Worth knowing:** A custom basket is non-representative, or representative but different from the initial basket used that business day. A “non-standard order” is an operational/commercial label, not a Rule 6c-11 category; unusual timing or processing alone does not make its basket custom."}}
